{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/InterfaceKernel.lean#L101-L133","doc":"**The closed form, for every `k`.** With `A = q - q⁻¹`,\n\n    `f A k * (q + q⁻¹) = q^k - (-1)^k * (q⁻¹)^k`.\n\nThe two terms are the `k`-th powers of the Hecke eigenvalues `q` and `-q⁻¹`,\nwhich are exactly the roots of the recursion's characteristic polynomial\n`t^2 - A t - 1` -- `A^2 + 4 = (q + q⁻¹)^2` is what makes them come out\nrational in `q` rather than involving a genuine square root. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.pow_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.pow_eq","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/InterfaceKernel.lean#L63-L85","doc":"**The interface identity.** In any commutative semiring, if `T` satisfies\nthe Hecke relation `T^2 = A*T + 1`, then every power of `T` is a linear\ncombination of `T` and `1` with the recursion's coefficients:\n\n    `T^(k+1) = f (k+1) * T + f k`\n\nInduction on `k` in two-step form: the `k+2` case rewrites `T^(k+2)` as\n`T^(k+1) * T`, applies the hypothesis twice, and closes by `ring` against the\ndefining recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.splitCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.splitCoeff","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/InterfaceKernel.lean#L57-L61","doc":"The coefficient LEFT BEHIND at the original grade -- the split weight.\n\nThis is the quantity the arc set out to bound. It is not bounded here, it is\nidentified: it is `f (k-1)`, exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.promoCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.promoCoeff","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/InterfaceKernel.lean#L54-L55","doc":"The coefficient that RIDES to grade +1 under one more crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_succ_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_succ_succ","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/InterfaceKernel.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_two","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/InterfaceKernel.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_one","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/InterfaceKernel.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f_zero","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/InterfaceKernel.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.InterfaceKernel.f","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/InterfaceKernel.lean#L37-L46","doc":"The alternating recursion `f 0 = 0`, `f 1 = 1`, `f (k+2) = A * f (k+1) + f k`.\n\nOver `ℤ[q,q⁻¹]` with `A = q - q⁻¹` its characteristic roots are `q` and `-q⁻¹`\n-- the two Hecke eigenvalues -- because `A^2 + 4 = (q + q⁻¹)^2`. That fact is\narchimedean-flavoured and is deliberately NOT stated here; see `discriminant`\nbelow for the ring-generic version of it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}